        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Piano Sonata No. 8\n- People: Sergei Prokofiev, Emil Gilels\n- Places: Moscow\n- Topics: first performances, Soviet pianists\n\nFacts:\n- Sergei Prokofiev's Piano Sonata No. 8 was first performed on 30 December 1944 in Moscow.\n- Emil Gilels gave the first performance of Sergei Prokofiev's Piano Sonata No. 8 on 30 December 1944 in Moscow.\n- Emil Grigoryevich Gilels was born on 19 October 1916 and died on 14 October 1985.\n- Emil Gilels was a Soviet pianist and is widely regarded as one of the greatest pianists of the 20th century.\n- Emil Gilels was sometimes transliterated as \"Hilels.\"",
